invariant: INV-36
file: tools/localize_macho.zig
catches: test/localize-check.sh
reason: the Mach-O localizer clears N_PEXT and leaves N_EXT set, so every
  symbol it moves into the local range stays external and the object exports
  it. The check compares the fixture's result with nmedit -s and llvm-objcopy
  -G on every host, so a Linux runner catches a Mach-O mistake too.

--- old
        if (class == .localized) symbol_table[i * nlist_size + 4] &= ~@as(u8, n_ext | n_pext);
--- new
        if (class == .localized) symbol_table[i * nlist_size + 4] &= ~@as(u8, n_pext);
